{"frame":{"request_id":"<sigma:1>","type":"control_request","request":{"subtype":"initialize","hooks":{"PreToolUse":[{"hookCallbackIds":["hook_0"]}],"PostCompact":[{"hookCallbackIds":["hook_1"]}]},"sdkMcpServers":["sigma"],"sdkMcpServerManifests":{"sigma":{"initializeResult":{"protocolVersion":"2025-11-25","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":true}},"serverInfo":{"name":"sigma","version":"1.0.0"}},"toolsListResult":{"tools":[{"name":"start_worker","description":"Starts a worker: an agent in a conversation of its own, which the user can open, watch and talk to, and which keeps working after your turn ends. Returns the worker's task name at once. Its final answer comes back through wait_worker, or as a message when you are not waiting.\nIf your task is `/root/task1` and you name a worker \"scout\", its task name is `/root/task1/scout`. You can call it `scout` or `/root/task1/scout`; other agents reach it by its full name.\nA worker runs on your provider and model unless you name others. Set `provider` and `model` only to what the user named, unchanged. The providers are script (a scripted model), claude (Claude Code), openai (ChatGPT). On your provider the worker has your tools and starts with your history, unless `fork_turns` is \"none\". On another provider it starts from your message alone, with none of your history or instructions, so write a complete brief; it runs that provider's default model when you name none.\nStart workers only when the user, or instructions such as AGENTS.md or a skill, ask for workers, delegation or parallel work.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"task_name":{"type":"string","description":"Name for the worker. Use lowercase letters, digits, and underscores."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The worker's task, in plain text."},"provider":{"type":"string","description":"The provider to run the worker on, exactly as the user named it: script, claude, openai. Omit to use yours."},"model":{"type":"string","description":"The model to run the worker on, exactly as the user named it. Omit to use yours, or the provider's default on another provider."},"effort":{"type":"string","enum":["minimal","low","medium","high","xhigh"],"description":"Reasoning effort for the worker. Omit to use yours."},"agent_type":{"type":"string","description":"Agent type for the worker, one your instructions list under Agent types. Omit unless explicitly asked."},"fork_turns":{"type":"string","enum":["all","none"],"description":"Your history to give the worker: \"all\", the default on your provider, or \"none\". A worker on another provider always starts with none."}},"required":["task_name","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"message_worker","description":"Sends a message to a worker, or to any agent of your tree by its task name. A working one reads it at its next step; an idle one reads it with its next task. Starts no new turn.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"target":{"type":"string","description":"The worker's task name, as start_worker returned it, or relative to yours."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The message to send."}},"required":["target","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"assign_worker","description":"Gives a worker a follow-up task, and starts it working if it is idle. A working worker takes the task at its next step. Its answer comes back through wait_worker.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"target":{"type":"string","description":"The worker's task name, as start_worker returned it, or relative to yours."},"message":{"type":"string","description":"The follow-up task."}},"required":["target","message"],"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"wait_worker","description":"Waits for your workers and returns what they sent: a finished worker's final answer, or a message from one. What it returns is not delivered to you again. Returns timed_out true when nothing arrives in time; call it again to keep waiting. Returns early, with nothing received, when the user sends new input.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"timeout_ms":{"type":"integer","minimum":-9007199254740991,"maximum":9007199254740991,"description":"Timeout in milliseconds. Defaults to 30000, min 10000, max 3600000."}},"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"list_workers","description":"Lists the agents of your tree, you and the workers under you, each by task name with whether it is running, done, interrupted or failed. Optionally filtered by task-name prefix.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"path_prefix":{"type":"string","description":"Task-name prefix, without a trailing slash. Omit to list them all."}},"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}},{"name":"stop_worker","description":"Stops a worker's current turn, if any, and returns its previous status. The worker stays available for messages and follow-up tasks.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","type":"object","properties":{"target":{"type":"string","description":"The worker's task name, as start_worker returned it, or relative to yours."}},"required":["target"],"additionalProperties":false},"execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"_meta":{"anthropic/alwaysLoad":true}}]}}},"appendSystemPrompt":"Workers. This session can start workers with the mcp__sigma__start_worker tool. A worker is an agent in a conversation of its own, which the user can open, watch and talk to. Start a worker when the user asks for one, or names a model or a provider for part of the work. Pass the provider and model they named, unchanged, in `provider` and `model`. When they name several, start one worker for each. With none named, leave `provider` out and the worker runs on your own models. For a quick helper inside your own turn, use your own subagent tool if you have one, or do the work yourself.","title":"Use the mcp__sigma__start_worker tool with task_name helper, provider script and message: Say hello. Then call mcp__sigma__wait_worker with timeout_ms 60000, and reply with exactly the text the worker sent."}},"type":"expect_outbound"}
